diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 344f452..5be06c9 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,7 +2,16 @@
 
 Pulse is an internal market-insights dashboard. It shows key figures, a sortable table of instruments, a watchlist, top movers and recent activity; the house portfolio with an allocation chart; a filterable, paginated trade blotter with a detail drawer; an instrument page with price history, key stats and recent trades; a searchable client list with a detail drawer and client notes; a list of daily reports with status badges; notifications in the top bar; and user settings (theme and notifications) saved in the browser.
 
-Routes: `/` dashboard, `/portfolio`, `/trades`, `/instruments/:symbol`, `/clients`, `/reports`, `/settings`.
+Routes: `/` dashboard, `/portfolio`, `/portfolio/print` (the printable statement, outside the app shell), `/trades`, `/instruments/:symbol`, `/clients`, `/reports`, `/settings`.
+
+Reports and money: report-style figures are whole dollars with a thousands separator (`$1,234,568`), through `formatWholeDollars`: the holdings table and its Total row, the client details drawer, the AUM in "Trades by client", the portfolio CSV and the print view. Compact amounts (`$31.2M`) stay in cards and lists.
+
+What is new:
+
+- Portfolio: a health score (0 to 100; up to 60 points for diversification plus 200 times the return on cost, each part rounded, the sum held to 0..100), "Top contributors" (top 10 by unrealized P&L in whole dollars, ties by name), "Export portfolio CSV" and a "Print view" link.
+- Dashboard: "Trades by client" (one aggregated row per client) and "New clients this month". A client can have several accounts (a closed one and its replacement); the name is the identity, and the data is frozen at 27 Oct 2026, so "this month" is October 2026.
+- Instrument page: "Daily trend", at most the latest 30 days, with optional From and To days.
+- Clients: closed accounts carry a "Closed" badge. Settings: switches use `--color-switch-on` in both themes.
 
 All data is mocked: typed fetchers in `src/api` read JSON files in `src/data` after a short artificial delay.
 
